  "messages": [
    {
      "sender": "SYSTEM",
      "recipient": "USER",
      "content": "{{USER_INSTRUCTION}}ROUND 1\nQuery: Delete the old text message from Charlie about the cancelled meeting, and update my 'Data Assignments' note to state that Alice handles Time-series charts and Bob handles Cross-sectional charts.\nInstructions: Ask the agent to delete the text message from Charlie regarding the cancelled meeting, and update your 'Data Assignments' note to reflect that Alice is responsible for time-series charts and Bob is responsible for cross-sectional charts. Since you have multiple notes with similar names (like Q1 and Q2), the agent should ask for clarification. When it does, specify that you want to update the 'Q2 Data Assignments' note. Wait for the agent to confirm the deletion and the note update before moving on.\n\nROUND 2 [provide: image_1, image_2, image_3, image_4, image_5]\nQuery: Here are the 5 charts. Check the note we just updated to confirm the assignments. Then, filter these charts based on their x-axis. For every single chart, send a separate text message to the correct person containing the chart's title. So if someone is assigned three charts, they should receive three individual text messages.\nInstructions: Provide the five chart images. Ask the agent to check the updated assignments note to determine who handles time-series charts (x-axis represents historical time) and who handles cross-sectional charts (x-axis does not represent historical time). Instruct the agent to filter the charts accordingly and send an individual text message for each chart to the appropriate person, with each message containing the title of the assigned chart. Emphasize that they should receive separate messages for each chart, not one combined message. If the agent asks for clarification on how to classify them, remind it to look at the x-axis of each chart. Conclude the conversation once all five messages have been sent.\n\nYou have 5 images available to share with the agent using the send_message_with_image tool.\nIMPORTANT: Image IDs are ZERO-INDEXED integers (0, 1, 2, ...). Do NOT add 1 to the IDs.\nAvailable image IDs: [0, 1, 2, 3, 4]\nImage mapping:\n  image_1.jpg -> image ID 0\n  image_2.jpg -> image ID 1\n  image_3.jpg -> image ID 2\n  image_4.jpg -> image ID 3\n  image_5.jpg -> image ID 4\n\n## IMAGE DELIVERY\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f IMPORTANT: You MUST use the `send_message_with_image` tool to share images with User B. Do NOT just describe images in text \u2014 you MUST call the tool.\n\nImage delivery schedule:\n\n  Round 2: YOU MUST call the send_message_with_image tool with image_ids='0,1,2,3,4' \u2014 do NOT write the tool name as text; use the actual function call. Include a natural, conversational message to the assistant."
    },
